	(uuid "aa8eb427-a80e-4e0f-8f48-447b7f7c56a1")
	(paper "A4")
	(lib_symbols)
	(text "FOR THE INSERT/FX CHAIN MATRIX:\nCD4067 x 48\n\n16 for Channel insert -> select insert line 1-16\n16 (one for each insert return) -> select another insert (1-15) or 0 go below\n16 From 0 out of previous mux -> select return channel 1-16\n\nUSE CD4094 SHIFT REGS TO WRITE THEM\n\nAnything that drives a CD4067 input also runs on ±8 V\n78L08 and a 79L08\n\nLevel-shift 3.3 V logic with an LM339\n\nCD4094s power up with random contents, which means random routes and possible source conflicts. To avoid this:\n\nPull every CD4067 inhibit line up to +8 V through about 100 kΩ, so every mux is off by default.\nHold the CD4094 output-enable low at power-up. Its outputs then float and the pull-ups keep all muxes disabled.\nThe comparator input for this line needs a pull-down on the microcontroller side, so the line stays\nlow while the microcontroller is in reset.\nAt boot, the firmware shifts in a known safe state, pulses strobe, and then raises output enable."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
